    "key_finding": "A 82-parameter ephemeris-like basis can strongly absorb or over-absorb a static synodic carrier on the real LLR sampling manifold (absorption 96.0% in the worst-case linear scenario). However, the dynamically modulated TEP signal's sideband-to-carrier ratio survives at 244.1% after fitting. On real INPOP19a residuals, the sideband-to-carrier ratio survives at 197.2%. The persistence of sideband structure under this high-dimensional linear stress test supports the interpretation that the residual signal carries a dynamical signature, not merely leakage from a partially absorbed static component. Moreover, the actual INPOP19a residuals exhibit \u03b7 = -3.18e-04, confirming that INPOP's own 100+ parameter fit did not absorb the signal. This proxy is a linear stress test, not a symplectic N-body integrator, and cannot emulate the iterative dynamic potentials of the actual Fortran/C++ code underlying INPOP or DE430. A source-level INPOP/DE430 refit with \u03b7 free remains the definitive absorption test."
